{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3169","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3169","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3169\",\"parent_revision\":\"6b9ce36b04c26c17a152ffe880d15af96af1d19da91c4838ede59413ea3e91e0\",\"root_revision\":\"6b9ce36b04c26c17a152ffe880d15af96af1d19da91c4838ede59413ea3e91e0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe need duplicate detection exists to serve is: before I spend effort researching and planning a problem, tell me whether that work already exists so I can extend it instead of repeating it. The current check does not serve that need, and each gap is independent of the others.\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-23: three items were created that duplicated items filed one to three minutes earlier by a concurrent session \u2014 #3139 duplicating #3138 (five seconds apart), #3143 duplicating #3141, #3144 duplicating #3140. The check ran on all three and reported no duplicate. Research and planning had already been spent on each.\\n\\n**It matches the wrong thing.** `_check_for_duplicates` in `backlog_core/operations.py` calls `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, items)`, which runs `difflib.SequenceMatcher` over normalised titles. That is character-sequence similarity on one field. Two authors describing the same defect choose different words, so the titles do not resemble each other even when the described problem is identical. Compare the pair that scored no match:\\n\\n- \\\"CI check for drift between MCP server tool lists and agent frontmatter `tools:` entries\\\"\\n- \\\"Agent `tools:` frontmatter drifts from MCP server tool lists with no enforcement and silent failure in both directions\\\"\\n\\nThe capability the need requires already exists in the same package: `backlog_list` accepts `search` and performs full-text matching across title, description, acceptance criteria and every section body, with AND/OR/NOT operators, regex, field-scoped terms, and `match_context` reporting where each term matched. The gate does not use it.\\n\\n**It fires at the wrong point in the lifecycle.** The check runs inside `add_item`, at creation. By then the research and planning the check exists to protect have already been spent \u2014 creation is the last step, not the first. The need is to know before investing, which means the check belongs at the point work is picked up, and its result has to reach whoever is about to start.\\n\\n**Its result cannot be acted on.** The check raises `DuplicateItemError` and the match tuple carries `(title, similarity_ratio, file_path)`. A file path is not a handle a caller can use to extend an item, and an exception offers only abort or `force`. To extend rather than duplicate, the caller needs the existing item's reference and enough of its content to judge whether the new information belongs there \u2014 which is the decision the user actually wants to make.\\n\\n**It reads a cache and reports absence as fact.** `GitHubBackend.list_work_items()` returns from the provider-private cache with no remote consultation; its own docstring says so, and the `backlog_list` tool defaults `from_github` to false. So an item created by another session and not yet pulled is invisible, and the check reports \\\"no duplicate\\\" rather than \\\"cannot tell\\\". `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` states the opposite as an invariant: \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results.\\\" That invariant is documented and this read path does not honour it. This gap is separate from the matching gap \u2014 fixing the matcher alone still misses a concurrent write.\\n\\nWhat a working check has to do, stated as outcomes rather than implementation: find an existing item that describes the same problem regardless of wording; run before effort is spent, not at write time; return the item so the caller can read it and decide to extend; and distinguish \\\"nothing matches\\\" from \\\"could not check\\\".\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 three duplicates created 2026-08-23 despite the check running\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## The Documented Workflow S Own Duplicate Step Is Not Executable On The Cli Path\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe create workflow (`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`) does specify content-based duplicate detection as Step 3, before the write:\\n\\n    backlog_list(search=\\\"{concept1} OR {concept2} OR {concept3}\\\", match_context=true)\\n\\nThat is the right check, and it is the capability the need requires. It is also MCP-only. The CLI's `backlog list` exposes `--label`, `--section`, `--status`, `--title`, `--type`, `--topic`, `--include-closed`, `--filter`, `--repo`, and `--refresh`. There is no `--search`, and `--title` is substring matching on one field \u2014 the same class of check as the fuzzy-title gate this issue is about.\\n\\nThe same workflow states that MCP and CLI are \\\"two equivalent interfaces to the same underlying `add_item()` operation\\\". For creation they are. For the duplicate detection that must precede it, they are not, and nothing on the CLI path says so.\\n\\nThat matters because the CLI is the fallback when the MCP write is unavailable. In the observed incident the MCP `backlog_add` call was rejected, the caller fell back to the CLI, and on that path the documented pre-write check had no implementation to call. The three duplicates followed.\\n\\nTwo consequences to weigh, beyond the four gaps above:\\n\\n- Either the CLI gains a `search` option with the same full-text semantics as the MCP parameter, or the workflow states that Step 3 requires the MCP interface and that the CLI path cannot satisfy it. Silent non-equivalence between two interfaces documented as equivalent is the defect either way.\\n- `--refresh` exists on the CLI and `from_github` exists on the MCP tool, both defaulting off. Whatever check is performed, it must refresh before concluding absence, or report that it could not check.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b7766185742fd04b45d648a8702c87d95d46bfad4af55cf1acd83022e37811c3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQOH1Eg\"}"}